(In simple terms: an item's rate is mostly its own history. The category average only counts like 30 extra days of) Tj
T* (data, so for an item with a full year of sales it barely changes anything. For an item that was never used, the rate) Tj
T* (comes out small \(a slow mover\), instead of pretending it sells like a typical item. This is called an empirical Bayes) Tj
T* (\(Gamma-Poisson\) estimate.) Tj
